      "review": "Make four focused corrections to the existing survey, preserving all nine source URLs and source labels. Apply them fully; do not keep the unsupported old sentences. All writing/checks inside sandbox.\n\n1. Replace the ENTIRE Background paragraph with a concise description of Sora's compressed spacetime latent patches and variable-duration/resolution training [1], and the Runway Gen-2 approach [2] only as supported by its official page. Remove the historical RNN/GAN claims, the broad claim that LLMs established generalist paradigms, and speculation about democratization. Primary URLs: https://openai.com/index/video-generation-models-as-world-simulators/ and https://www.runwayml.com/research/scale-speed-and-stepping-stones-the-path-to-gen-2 .\n2. Replace the ENTIRE Trends and open problems paragraph with three cited, supported directions: Open-Sora reported $200k training and efficiency/reproducibility [7]; CogVideoX text-video alignment/temporal coherence [6]; WorldGuide closed-loop procedural execution versus open-loop and long-horizon state tracking [8]. Remove unsupported claims about replacing rigid pipelines, causal tokenizers, and fractions of proprietary cost. Primary URL: https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12459 .\n3. In the comparative section, replace the statement attributing pretrained image backbones jointly to NExT-GPT and Open-Sora. Say NExT-GPT connects pretrained modality encoders/decoders with an LLM [4], while Open-Sora initializes from FLUX [7]. Distinguish each model architecture; do not ascribe expert transformers to all three latent diffusion systems.\n4. Remove the ~300,000 vocabulary-size statement from VideoPoet: retain only the source-supported decoder-only autoregressive multimodal framework [5]. Do not introduce numerical details without retrieved evidence.\n\nKeep all other supported content. No editorial correction notes, cite substantial text, rerun finalizer and validator. Do not change source provenance to meet the rubric.\n",
      "before_report_sha256": "f44111c87e0b12863632095798ec417dae8c46782cc8deff4070fef6da04c31e"
